acatchtray.cpp
- DoCatchTray cases 500 / 600: Type_HT9050 calls W906_CatchFromEmpty9050 (end of file) instead of golden CatchNewTrayFromBuffer:
  W906_ProbeEmpty9050 counts the Empty stack when unknown (-1): MEmptyZ from the deepest layer not below Home upwards until
  SenEmptySelectHasTray -> L+1 trays; a tray already at the deepest layer -> MES1022; none but SnEmptyDrawerHasTray on -> MES1024;
  SIM = 5. Then DoCatchFromEmpty_9050 (no caller in 910). Count 0 -> answers 2 (DoCatchTray back to case 1), MES1021 every 100th
  call, RETRY re-probes. Same 0/1/2 answers as CatchNewTrayFromBuffer.
- DoCatchFromEmpty_9050 takes the TOP tray (Up[n-1]) and makes n-1 (910 never changed the count); the place into Empty waits for a
  known count (:4398).
- DoCatchTray 400 / 1000 / 2000 also re-init the 9050 sub-cursors (InitialCatchFromEmpty_9050 / InitialPlaceToAuto_9050 /
  InitialPlaceToBuffer_9050).
cmydef.cpp: iAuto1..3LayerCount_9050 start at 0 (= empty) instead of -1 (the first place went one pitch above the base).
asendic_Loader.cpp DoLoadNewICTray_9050: Loader count 0 raises MES0920 (RETRY / CLEAN OUT) and sets -1 so DoLoad_9050 re-probes --
  was a silent 1 -> 800 -> 900 -> 1 loop.
csystem.cpp InitAllProcessTask (HOME / START): HT9050 also calls W906_InitTrayTasks9050 (Loader / Empty / Buffer / NewICTray cursors,
  Empty re-probe).
Not changed: DoPlaceTrayToAuto_9050's 'push the existing stack aside' branch (would add 2 layers per place; waits for EastSun).
Other machines: golden. Same lines + end of file.
tests: test_flow9050_tray.cpp -- the three 910 pins updated to the new behaviour, new [CW] block (5 checks); test_fp9050_index.cpp [F2]
census also exempts iTestYFinePitchTask, read by csystem.cpp W906_FlowTraceTick (FLOWTRACE, op-log only).
Flow9050_Tray 115/115, W6_3_CatchTray, Flow9050_Shuttle, W6_6_Hub, W6_6_CSystemCycle, FP9050_Pure, FP9050_Index, HT9050_ShtSafe,
HT9050_DryRun, HT9050_ProdFlow, E044TorqueWait passed. Debug linked, release linked. Backups D:\HT9045\_review\*.bak_trayflow9050_20261007_233435.
